    "md5": "07c54d8aa270f2f7ec1bb705c0b82b50",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1533,
    "chunk_text": "Anna Weerakoon Karunatilleke as Sri Lanka\u2019s ambassador for Maritime SheEO.\n\nAnna Weerakoon Karunatilleke has spent her career breaking barriers in one of the world\u2019s most traditionally male-dominated sectors. Having made history as Sri Lanka\u2019s first female Marine Engineer, her recent appointment as an Ambassador for Maritime SheEO marks the latest chapter in a life dedicated to technical excellence and social progress.\n\nMaritime SheEO is a global community dedicated to empowering women leaders across the maritime sector. Through high-impact conferences, a structured mentorship programme, and a community of over 800 members, the organisation provides tangible leadership pathways for everyone from students to CXOs. Notably, its dedicated research wing produces data-driven insights to inform policy, including a significant 2025 study on the inclusion of women in the Sri Lankan maritime industry. By offering a free, community-led platform, Maritime SheEO ensures that access to opportunity is never a barrier to driving systemic change.\n\nAnna\u2019s influence extends far beyond the shipyard; she is a published author and an international speaker who has consistently contributed to global conversations on maritime safety and gender inclusion.\n\nContinuing investor optimism over Q3 corporate results helps retain CSE\u2019s glow\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
