    "chunk_text": "Dialog introduces Blackview 5G Smartphone and Tablet to advance digital inclusion\n\nDialog Axiata PLC, Sri Lanka\u2019s #1 connectivity provider, has announced the introduction of two new affordable Blackview 5G devices to expand access to next-generation technology, reinforcing its commitment to democratising digital connectivity and accelerating digital transformation by enabling more Sri Lankans to experience the capabilities of Dialog 5G Ultra, Sri Lanka\u2019s largest 5G network.\n\nBuilding on the momentum created with Dialog\u2019s recent launch of affordable devices, the new Blackview Shark 6 5G features a 6.88-inch HD+ IPS display with a 120Hz refresh rate and an octa-core 5G Unisoc T8100 processor. It also offers 4GB + 128GB memory with 8GB RAM expansion, a 5000mAh battery with 18W fast charging, 8MP front and 16MP rear cameras, an 18-month warranty, a Dialog data bundle and availability across 600+ outlets.\n\nComplementing the smartphone, the Blackview Zeno 10 5G tablet delivers a robust and versatile user experience with its 11-inch FHD+ IPS display featuring a 90Hz refresh rate, UNISOC T8200 5G-ready chipset, 6GB RAM with up to 12GB virtual RAM, 128GB storage expandable to 2TB, 8,800mAh battery, 16MP rear and 13MP front cameras, and Android 15 with DokeOS 4.0. The tablet comes bundled with a case, screen protector, wireless keyboard, earphones and stylus, and includes dual-SIM & 5G connectivity, 18-month warranty and a Dialog data bundle.\n\nCSE donates LKR 25 million to post-Ditwah \u201cRebuilding Sri Lanka\u201d fund\n\nTurkey\u2019s foreign policy seen as vital to navigate current world instability\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
