    "chunk_text": "This was an opening for him to talk about Shirley Amerasinghe\u2019s contribution to the Law of the Sea Convention. And he concluded by saying that Lalith was the brightest he had met of the Ceylonese. And then he sprung the question.\n\nAfter about 40 minutes of very interesting conversation, including the invasion of Iraq by Bush Jnr, it was time to go. We both got up.\n\nHe smiled, shook hands across the table, and said, \u201cJavier Perez de Cuellier from Peru\u201d. I was dumbfounded. I had been chatting to the 83 -year old former Secretary General of the UN.\n\nPerez de Cuellier died in 2020, aged 100. De Cuellier was a two term UN chief who brokered the peace agreement between Iran and Iraq in 1988.\n\nThat the night, I shared a bottle of champagne with my teetotaller wife at our apartment.\n\n(Excerpted from an anthology of memoirs by Nihal Kodituwakku) \u270d\ufe0f\n\nEmpowering the next generation: A vision for students\u2019 leadership in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
