    "chunk_text": "We often associate elected representatives, or public servants, with the term public office. But I will use this term in a broader sense today. For the purposes of today\u2019s talk, I include within the idea any office that requires the person holding that office to exercise power or authority under public law. This description would cover members of Parliament, the President, members of the Judiciary, the police and public servants. In the Sri Lankan context, it would also include university academics and members of what we commonly describe as independent commissions such as the Human Rights Commission and the Election Commission."
