    "md5": "17d4ab1a88445dc36ddc18d38c70000b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1786,
    "chunk_text": "INFRACON 2026 to drive future of infrastructure and construction development in Sri Lanka\n\nThe Infrastructure and Construction Exhibition (INFRACON 2026), a premier industry event dedicated to the nation\u2019s infrastructure and construction sectors, will take place from 3 to 5 July at the Sirimavo Bandaranaike Memorial Exhibition Centre (SBMEC), Colombo.\n\nOrganised by Lanka Exhibitions and Conference Services Ltd., (Winner of multiple presidential awards in the MICE category and inductee into the MICE Hall of Fame) and Savor International Ltd., from Bangladesh, who is also an industry leader in the MICE sector in Bangladesh.\n\nINFRACON 2026 will bring together industry leaders, policymakers, developers, contractors, engineers, architects, and technology providers. The event will feature organisations and suppliers from 5 major sectors - HVAC-R and Cold Chain, Power and Energy, Green Grid, Safe Water, and Build Materials. These major sectors will be showcased within the exhibition as individual concurrent segments. INFRACON 2026 will serve as a catalyst for growth and collaboration in Sri Lanka\u2019s rapidly evolving infrastructure landscape, with participation from leading local and international exhibitors, shaping the future of infrastructure development in Sri Lanka and the South Asian region.\n\nWith strong participation expected from government institutions, private sector organisations, international brands, and trade delegations, INFRACON 2026 aims to foster collaboration across sectors and position Sri Lanka as a regional hub for infrastructure development. With 200 expected exhibitors and over 5,000 trade visitors, the exhibition reaffirms its position as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most significant platforms for the infrastructure and construction industries."
  },
