    "chunk_text": "With strong participation expected from government institutions, private sector organisations, international brands, and trade delegations, INFRACON 2026 aims to foster collaboration across sectors and position Sri Lanka as a regional hub for infrastructure development. With 200 expected exhibitors and over 5,000 trade visitors, the exhibition reaffirms its position as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most significant platforms for the infrastructure and construction industries.\n\nThis three-day event aims to serve as a platform that showcases the latest innovations, products, services, and technologies related to infrastructure development, construction materials, heavy machinery, power and energy, smart buildings, urban development, and engineering solutions.\n\nINFRACON 2026 is more than an exhibition, it is a knowledge sharing and networking platform that supports\u00a0 Sri Lanka\u2019s vision for resilient, sustainable and future-ready infrastructure. Visitors will have the chance to engage with exhibitors through live demonstrations, product launches, and interactive displays showcasing modern, sustainable construction solutions.\n\nLanka Exhibition and Conference Services, a leading trade exhibition organiser have tied up with Bangladesh\u2019s premier exhibition management company Savor International to team up and bring this event to Sri Lanka. The event is supported by the Solar Industries Association (SIA) and ASHRAE Sri Lanka Chapter, which is the body for the heating, ventilation, AC and refrigeration sector in Sri Lanka."
