    "chunk_text": "Samsung Sri Lanka Managing Director SangHwa Song said: \u201cThis Superbrands recognition is a strong affirmation of the trust Sri Lankan consumers place in Samsung. It reflects our relentless focus on innovation, quality, and long-term value, as well as our commitment to bringing world-class technology to Sri Lanka. We are honoured to be recognised as a brand that consumers genuinely choose and believe in.\u201d\n\nThis Superbrands recognition comes at a time when the company continues to strengthen its leadership across Consumer Electronics and Smart living solutions. Globally, Samsung has retained its position as the No.1 TV manufacturer for 19 consecutive years, driven by leadership in immersive viewing experiences and enhanced connection and security. Sri Lankan consumers benefit directly from this global expertise through access to Samsung\u2019s latest Neo QLED, OLED, and Lifestyle TV ranges.\n\nSamsung continues to set benchmarks with intelligent, energy-efficient, and durable products designed for modern lifestyles. The brand\u2019s 20-year warranty on Digital Inverter Motors and Compressors stands as a testament to product reliability and long-term performance, offering consumers unmatched peace of mind and reinforcing Samsung\u2019s confidence in its engineering excellence.\n\nSamsung\u2019s connected ecosystem is powered by SmartThings, an open platform that enables seamless integration across Digital Appliances. SmartThings allows users to monitor, control, and automate their homes with ease, enhancing convenience, efficiency, and energy management. Complementing this ecosystem is Samsung Knox Security, a defence-grade security platform that safeguards devices, data, and connected environments, reinforcing Samsung\u2019s commitment to privacy and digital trust."
  },
