    "chunk_text": "Samsung\u2019s connected ecosystem is powered by SmartThings, an open platform that enables seamless integration across Digital Appliances. SmartThings allows users to monitor, control, and automate their homes with ease, enhancing convenience, efficiency, and energy management. Complementing this ecosystem is Samsung Knox Security, a defence-grade security platform that safeguards devices, data, and connected environments, reinforcing Samsung\u2019s commitment to privacy and digital trust.\n\nEnsuring global innovation is accessible locally remains central to Samsung Sri Lanka\u2019s strategy. By providing easy payment plans in partnership with leading banks, Samsung enables more Sri Lankan consumers to experience premium global technology, reinforcing its position as a brand that understands local needs while delivering international standards.\n\nBeyond consumer recognition, Superbrands status delivers wide-ranging benefits across the business ecosystem. It provides powerful validation for all stakeholders including customers, retailers, suppliers, investors, and employees, reaffirming that Samsung is a well-managed brand with enduring value. Inclusion in the Superbrands publication offers high-profile exposure among Sri Lanka\u2019s top corporate leaders and marketing professionals, while reinforcing employee pride and strengthening the brand\u2019s employer value proposition.\n\nSamsung Sri Lanka\u2019s leadership team, including the Managing Director and Director and Head of Consumer Electronics, attended the Superbrands Tribute Ceremony held on 12 January at Hilton, marking this milestone alongside the country\u2019s most respected brand custodians."
