    "chunk_size_bytes": 1559,
    "chunk_text": "EDB unveils flagship statistical publication \u2018Export Performance Indicators 2024\u2019\n\nAt the official launch of the \u2018Export Performance Indicators 2024\u2019 were (from left): EDB Acting Additional Director General (Development) Kumudinie Mudalige, Chairman and CEO Mangala Wijesinghe, Digital Economy Deputy Minister Eng. Eranga Weeraratne, Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti and Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Central Bank Governor Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Chief Adviser to the President on Digital Economy Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, and Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma\n\nThe Export Development Board (EDB) has launched its flagship annual publication \u2018Export Performance Indicators 2024\u2019.\n\nThe latest edition provides statistical information related to Sri Lanka\u2019s external trade and its contribution to major economic indicators such as trade balance.\u00a0 GDP and individual sectorial involvement for the year 2024 and five preceding years.\n\nThis volume is the 38th Volume of this publication, and its previous editions have been constantly used as a comprehensive and trustworthy reference by exporters, researchers and policy makers.\n\nThe data compiled in the \u2018Export Performance Indicators 2024\u2019, is presented along with the trade statistics for the last 05 years along with a comprehensive analysis of Sri Lanka\u2019s export trade, products and services, from the year 2020 up to the year 2024, including the export regions per each product, their market growth and projected export forecast."
