    "md5": "92ee5bd8d5e9218677de03f04078f260",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1826,
    "chunk_text": "Nawaloka Hospitals pioneers in AI-driven healthcare, announced as Platinum Sponsor of Medicare 2026\n\nMedicare 2026 Organising Committee\u00a0 Chairperson and Asia Wellness Forum President Dr. Amal Harsha de Silva, Nawaloka Hospitals PLC\u00a0 Director/General Manager\u00a0 Prof. Lal Chandrasena and Nawaloka Hospitals PLC Senior Manager Operations Kanishka Warusavitarana\u00a0 at the sponsor handing over occasion\n\nNawaloka Hospitals PLC, a pioneer in Sri Lanka\u2019s private healthcare sector, is taking a bold step into the future by integrating Artificial Intelligence (AI) into healthcare. Demonstrating its commitment to advancing medical innovation, the hospital group will proudly serve as the Platinum Sponsor of the 15th edition of the Medicare \u2013 International Healthcare Exhibition 2026, where it will unveil its latest AI-driven technologies.\n\nThe three-day exhibition, scheduled from 6 to 8 March 2026 at the Sirimavo Bandaranaike Memorial Exposition Centre (BMICH), Colombo, is widely recognised as the nation\u2019s premier platform for healthcare advancement, knowledge exchange, and industry collaboration.\n\nWith Nawaloka Hospital Holdings PLC\u2019s unwavering dedication to healthcare excellence, its role as a lead partner strengthens Medicare 2026\u2019s vision of shaping a healthier future for Sri Lanka. Visitors will gain unique insights into the practical applications of AI in clinical practice and its transformative impact on healthcare delivery.\n\nSince its inception, Nawaloka Hospital has led the introduction of advanced medical technology in Sri Lanka \u2014 from pioneering the nation\u2019s first CT scanner to now embracing AI-driven healthcare solutions. The hospital is developing AI-powered CT, MRI, OCD, and cardiac scanners for early, non-invasive disease detection, delivering faster and more accurate diagnostics."
  },
