    "chunk_size_bytes": 1256,
    "chunk_text": "Election Commission invites applications for political party recognition in 2026\n\nThe Election Commission has invited applications from political parties seeking official recognition for 2026.\n\nThe Commission said applications will be accepted from 28 January to 28 February. Submissions must be made using the prescribed application form and supported by the required documentation, signed by the party Secretary.\n\nApplication forms are available through the Election Commission\u2019s official website, district election offices, and the Office of the Election Secretary.\n\nThe Commission said recognised political parties will be required to specify their approved symbol in line with relevant Gazette notifications.\n\nApplicants must submit supporting documents including the party constitution, a list of office bearers, details of female office bearers during the past four years, audited financial statements, the party\u2019s current policy statement, and evidence of continuous political activity over the previous four years.\n\nCompleted applications must be submitted either by post or by hand to the Election Commission on or before 3 p.m. on 28 February. Submissions must be clearly marked \u2018Application for Recognition of Political Party \u2013 2026.\u2019"
  },
