    "md5": "555e9322cc8b86d5bc19d7c7b72fcf9a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThat\u2019s how they wanted us to do it, okay?\u201d I replied defensively, justifying what, in her opinion, was one of the most unfortunate hairstyles of the twenty-first century.\n\n\u201cOur school,\u201d I said, knowing fully well that someone who could voluntarily wear pajamas to school had no real concept of how extreme, sometimes absurd our school system could be.\n\nA few years ago, I used to see an elderly couple, both around 80, on my walk home from college every other day. They would sit under a tree on Adirondack chairs in their garden, facing the street, which felt like a rare sight. Over time, their friendly smiles turned into small talk.\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s too boring inside the house, and it\u2019s summer,\u201d the older woman would say, almost as if she needed to justify their presence outdoors.\n\n\u201cI\u2019d do the same,\u201d I\u2019d reply, perhaps because they reminded me so much of my own grandmother. She would sit on her small chair beneath the ambarella tree in our garden, which she claimed was older than she was, gazing over the yard for hours. Sometimes I\u2019d join her, curious about what held her attention, but I could never last more than 15 minutes before growing restless. But now I realize that may have been her quiet form of therapy, her daily dose of serenity, being in touch with nature and reminiscing about years she believed were behind her.\n\nAs time passed, I noticed that many of my school friends, like me, are scattered across different countries soon after graduating, a trend that\u2019s only grown stronger in recent years. When we talk now, the one common thread is how much we miss the simple act of planning to hang out, something that has since become occasion worthy. We often laugh about childhood stories, like the afternoon one of our daredevil friends fell into an abandoned pond at school while searching for the \u201cgoldfish\u201d she claimed to have seen the day before."
