    "chunk_size_bytes": 1434,
    "chunk_text": "There is also a cultural component. Binge watching entire seasons of a popular series has become a shared social experience. People talk about the latest shows with friends, coworkers, and on social media. This creates a cultural pressure to watch certain shows quickly. People do not want to be left out of conversations about plot twists or character developments. In the same way, social media habits can be fueled by the desire to stay up to date. Friends may post photos from events, share opinions on current news, or post humorous content. Users are motivated to keep up with these posts so they feel connected and informed. Missing out can make people feel excluded or out of sync with their social circles.\n\nThere are positive aspects to these behaviors as well. Watching a series that resonates with a person can provide joy, relaxation, and a shared cultural experience. Social media can help people stay in touch and share meaningful moments. It can also be a source of inspiration and information. However, the negative impacts should not be ignored. Excessive screen time can interfere with sleep, reduce face to face interaction, and contribute to feelings of anxiety. Binge watching late at night can disrupt healthy sleep patterns. Constant scrolling on social media can create unrealistic comparisons that affect self esteem. These harmful effects can lead to a feeling of regret or dissatisfaction over wasted time."
