    "md5": "22e85523a93d47517179e51190102412",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1742,
    "chunk_text": "A Southern Voice, a Northern Story:\n\nUthuru Kon\u00e7 Arumasia (The Wonder at the Northern Corner), a book in Sinhala language by Dr. Viduni Basnayake, was launched on Sunday, January 25, 2026, at the Auditorium of the Clinical Research and Training Block (CTRB), Faculty of Medicine, University of Jaffna. The event was co-organised by the Medical Students\u2019 Union, Student Wellbeing Centre, and the Department of Community and Family Medicine, Faculty of Medicine, University of Jaffna.\n\nDr. Basnayake is a proud alumna of the Jaffna Medical Faculty. She graduated in January 2025 and is currently completing her internship at Teaching Hospital Jaffna. Originally from Kandy, her first Sinhala book, Uthuru Kon\u00e7 Arumasia (The Wonder at the Northern Corner) was born in late 2019, during her second year of medical studies. It is a heartfelt chronicle of the six unforgettable years (2019-2024) she spent as a medical student walking through the Northern Peninsula.\n\nThrough lived experience, careful observation, reflective inquiry and emotion, Dr. Basnayake invites the reader to journey alongside her across an extraordinary range of themes\u2014from the Jaffna train and the historic Jaffna Fort to Delft Island, Point Pedro and Mannar; from the region\u2019s rich food, culture, to the remnants of King Sangiliyan\u2019s kingdom; from vintage cars and the donkeys of Mannar, to the legacy of American missionaries; from Nallur and other sacred temples to the iconic Jaffna Library, and much more. The prose goes beyond sharing information. With a rhythmic quality, blending poetry and vivid imagery, the book traces, step by step, landscapes and lives, memories and quiet transformations that define the region beyond what is often seen or spoken."
