    "chunk_text": "Through lived experience, careful observation, reflective inquiry and emotion, Dr. Basnayake invites the reader to journey alongside her across an extraordinary range of themes\u2014from the Jaffna train and the historic Jaffna Fort to Delft Island, Point Pedro and Mannar; from the region\u2019s rich food, culture, to the remnants of King Sangiliyan\u2019s kingdom; from vintage cars and the donkeys of Mannar, to the legacy of American missionaries; from Nallur and other sacred temples to the iconic Jaffna Library, and much more. The prose goes beyond sharing information. With a rhythmic quality, blending poetry and vivid imagery, the book traces, step by step, landscapes and lives, memories and quiet transformations that define the region beyond what is often seen or spoken.\n\nThe book launch was well attended, with over 100 persons present. After the welcome address by Prof. R. Surenthirakumaran, Dean, Faculty of Medicine, University of Jaffna, the author shared her motivation for writing the book, while gratefully acknowledging her parents and sister, who were present at this joyous occasion. Dr. Basnayake thanked her parents for their quiet but powerful presence in her life, and their unwavering trust in her work and the freedom they gave her to make her life decisions.\n\nNext, the author was felicitated by Prof. Gitanjali Sathiadas, Chair Professor of Paediatrics, Department of Paediatrics, University of Jaffna, who was also invited to receive the first book. Following the presentation of the book to many others present, including staff of the University and Teaching Hospital Jaffna, the 45th Batch of medical students took to the stage, performing a spirited fusion dance, keeping with the book\u2019s theme."
