    "md5": "45ce5686b294625ddae293ce99ec87f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1916,
    "chunk_text": "Sad Day for Sri Lanka Navy Special Boat Squadron\n\nA Few months ago, he was in the headlines as the first Sri Lankan to win the US Navy SEAL Commando Trident badge. Lt. Koyan Chamitha of the elite Special Boat Squadron (SBS) achieved this unique honour by successfully completing the SEAL BUDs course at the US Navy SEAL training school in the US. This is considered one of the toughest commando training courses in the World. Koyan joined 200 US Navy personnel and candidates of other friendly navies for 14 months of unbelievable training, the worst part being the \u201cHell week\u201d: trainees are NOT ALLOWED TO SLEEP FOR ONE WEEK and are made to do rigorous training in mud flats of San Diego beachfront of California, bordering Mexico.\n\nSEAL means training for unconventional warfare at sea\u2013\u2013all SEALs are combat divers), air\u2013\u2013all SEALs are paratroopers\u2013\u2013and land warfare, including maritime, jungle, urban and Arctic terrains.\n\nOut of 200 trainees, only 27 finally qualified to proudly wear the SEAL pin-Trident pin on their uniform! Koyan was one of them; he brought honour to SBS, the Sri Lanka Navy and the country.\n\nThe writer with Koyan on 01 November 2025 at the SBS HQ, Nicholson Cove, Naval Base, Trincomalee. He cofounded SBS with late Commander (VNF) Cedric Martinstyn in 1993 and commanded the elite naval unit twice during war.\n\nWhen he returned to Sri Lanka last year, SBS leadership entrusted to him the task of training officers/sailors who volunteered for a new batch of SBS trainees. Last week, he interacted with US Navy SEALs at Trincomalee in the SBS/ US Navy SEALs joint exercise named \u201cExercise Balance Style\u201d.\n\nSoon after the joint exercise, he travelled to Colombo to participate in the Independence Day Parade scheduled on 4 February 2026 at Independence Square.\n\nHe stayed with other SBS officers and sailors taking part in parade rehearsals at the Naval Base at Welisara."
