    "chunk_text": "Soon after the joint exercise, he travelled to Colombo to participate in the Independence Day Parade scheduled on 4 February 2026 at Independence Square.\n\nHe stayed with other SBS officers and sailors taking part in parade rehearsals at the Naval Base at Welisara.\n\nHe was found dead in his cabin in the Welisara Wardroom (Officers\u2019 Mess) the following morning\u2014possibly a silent heart attack in sleep. The complete postmortem reports will come out soon.\n\nThe joint training with the US Navy SEALs started in 1996, exactly 30 years ago. The SBS conducted this joint training every year, except two years when it had to commit all its troops to fighting LTTE terrorists.\n\nWhen we started joint training with US Navy SEALs, 30 years ago, our dream was to train one of the SBS officers at the San Diego US Navy Special Forces School. It took three decades for us to achieve that dream.\n\nOur own Navy Special Boats Squadron SEAL, 24-year-old Koyan went away \u201clike a candle in the wind\u201d.\n\nWV, RWP and Bar, RSP, VSV, USP, NI (M) (Pakistan), ndc, psn, Bsc\n\nSri Lanka Through Loving Eyes:A Call to Fix What Truly Matters\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
