    "md5": "90fc0165c03bb379113dd8b422a1066d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1736,
    "chunk_text": "Two Loyal, Noble Beings\n\nAs reported by Jeffrey Fettleman and Maya Taleki in conversation with the bold PM of Denmark in Greenland, Mette Frederiksen, Denmark\u2019s leader, has taken big risks standing up to President Trump. The first incident they narrate is how this intrepid woman, then a school girl, stood up to a pack of skinheads who bullied some immigrants and got socked in her jaw. She never tolerated bullies since. As the authors say, she ducked a punch, a big one, from no less a person that Donald Trump.\n\nYes, you know all about that. Even before he was voted in as Pres of the US, Trump said he would annex Greenland for the US as a defence strategy, never mind it was governed by Denmark as an autonomous region moving from being a colony of the Kingdom of Denmark. He has repeatedly said he would even buy Greenland from Denmark. In a speech to the world\u2019s financial elite at Davos, Trump said he would not use force to acquire that country. Later he said that NATO leaders and he had worked out \u201cthe framework of a future deal\u201d that would \u201cmake everyone happy.\u201d Why he mellowed was because of Congressional opposition and falling stock markets back home.\n\nFor months, Ms. Frederiksen has played a nervous game of brinkmanship with Mr. Trump, and it looks like she has won \u2014 for the moment. She has strongly refused the use of military bases in Greenland under the US sovereignty, excluding other nations. She has taken many risk with Trump. She may win.\n\nMy title said Two loyal, noble beings. Yes, one is a woman, the other \u2013 a dog. Maybe you guessed correct. Its Aloka the dog who has trotted more than 2000 km across several states in the US from Texas to Washington DC to be reached in early February."
  },
