    "chunk_size_bytes": 1464,
    "chunk_text": "My title said Two loyal, noble beings. Yes, one is a woman, the other \u2013 a dog. Maybe you guessed correct. Its Aloka the dog who has trotted more than 2000 km across several states in the US from Texas to Washington DC to be reached in early February.\n\nThe dog \u2013 his doggesness, his loyalty and such admirable qualities bought over from previous births. His fame he earned by accompanying 19 Buddhist monks on their Walk for Peace which has been world news for so many days now.\n\nAloka means light, He is no guiding light or lead. He is a follower but ever so loyal and committed to his task. Bhikkhu Pannakkara is the leader of the march. Aloka can be the show and most popular of the lot. Their message is of course peace but convey the messages of compassion, healing and universal connection, so needed in this world. The Americans of all types, mostly materialistic, have been very impressed and crowded round the monks who receive alms and speak to the people gathered.\n\nAloka got a dog disease in his foot and was still walking with the monks. They stopped and arranged for medical treatment. Before long he was again with them. His commitment so strong. He is a mongrel from India who follows momks on marches and managed to enter the States in spite of Trump.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
