    "md5": "44372f53b36a517bcc6d4b6d25a77726",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "Ceylinco Life first to open eco-friendly branch on company land in Ambalantota\n\nLife insurance market leader Ceylinco Life has strengthened its footprint in Sri Lanka\u2019s deep south with the opening of a new purpose-built, eco-friendly branch in Ambalantota, becoming the first life insurer in the area to operate from its own company-owned building.\n\nLocated at No. 207G, Tangalle Road, Ambalantota, the two-storey building is the 35th such company-owned branch building of Ceylinco Life. Purpose-designed to prioritise customer comfort while minimising environmental impact, the new branch reflects Ceylinco Life\u2019s long-term commitment to sustainable infrastructure development, the Company said.\n\nThe modern facility has a total gross floor area of 3,200 square feet, provides parking for 10 vehicles and was completed over a period of 11 months. The building has been constructed using precast concrete technology introduced by the National Engineering Research and Development Centre, offering significant advantages over traditional construction methods, including a 10 to 15 per cent cost saving, a 20 per cent reduction in construction time, high thermal comfort and lower long-term maintenance costs.\n\nDesigned in line with Ceylinco Life\u2019s green building concept, the Ambalantota branch operates with a 15 kW off-grid solar power system, enabling a zero electricity bill and eliminating the need for a diesel generator. The building also incorporates a rainwater harvesting system and a waste-water recycling system that supplies treated water for toilet flushing and gardening, while ensuring minimal use of pipe-borne water.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
