    "chunk_text": "NDB recognised as best women-friendly workplace\n\nNational Development Bank PLC (NDB) has been honoured as a Best Women-Friendly Workplace at the prestigious Great HR Awards 2025.\n\nThe award, presented by the Chartered Institute of Personnel Management Sri Lanka in collaboration with Mercer, recognises NDB\u2019s long-standing commitment to empowering women and fostering an inclusive culture at all organisational levels.\n\nThis accolade reinforces the strategic priority NDB places on gender inclusivity, reflected in its leadership development and employee experience. The bank\u2019s commitment is further validated by its EDGE Certification for gender equity, an international benchmark it has achieved for three consecutive years\u2014the only local organisation to do so.\n\n\u201cAt NDB, we believe that diversity strengthens us, inclusion defines us, and empowering women elevates us,\u201d said Lasantha Dasanayaka, Vice President \u2013 Human Resources.\n\nThe award underscores NDB\u2019s position as a leading employer committed to progressive people practices and holistic talent development in Sri Lanka.\n\nBrowns Hotels & Resorts brings a century of tea heritage to life at Newburgh Ella\n\nBitget hits $18B in tokenised stock trading as institutions drive growth\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
