    "md5": "094e8681fbed1600cc5827694a59c807",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1110,
    "chunk_text": "Bitget hits $18B in tokenised stock trading as institutions drive growth\n\nA new Messari report reveals Bitget has processed $18 billion in tokenized stock futures volume, with institutional traders dominating its spot market.\n\nThe research highlights a structural shift on the platform, where 82% of spot trading volume now comes from professional firms. Tokenized equities, launched in July 2025, have become a fastest-growing segment, with $13.6 billion traded in November alone.\n\n\u201cTokenized equities are moving from experimentation to real market structure,\u201d said Bitget CEO Gracy Chen, noting demand for continuous, on-chain access to traditional assets.\n\nTesla led trading with over $6.3 billion in volume. East Asia accounts for 39.6% of activity, with growing interest from Latin America and Europe. The data underscores a global trend toward consolidated platforms for both digital and traditional assets.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
