    "md5": "7fdb89dc9e283110172efd6ac4f9b94a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1361,
    "chunk_text": "CC meets tomorrow to consider President\u2019s nomination for AG\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has re-nominated a candidate for AG\n\nThe Constitutional Council (CC) is to meet early this week to consider the re-submission of Senior Deputy Auditor General L.S.I. Jayarathne for appointment as Auditor General (AG).\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has re-nominated Jayarathne after her name was earlier rejected by the Council.\n\nAccording to sources, the CC is scheduled to meet tomorrow (3) at 2 p.m. to reconsider the President\u2019s nomination for the post of AG.\n\nHowever, the re-submission follows the withdrawal of the nomination of Open University Bursar W.M.K.P.A. Wickremesinghe, whose name had been proposed previously.\n\nAlthough the newly appointed CC members \u2013 Austin Fernando, Prof. Wasantha Seneviratne, and Ranjith Ariyaratna \u2013 met on Friday, they have not taken a decision on the appointment, which has been vacant for nearly nine months since the retirement of Chulantha Wickramaratne.\n\nSenior officer Dharmapala Gammanpila was appointed as Acting AG but was not nominated for the permanent post. Earlier, three names were proposed but the CC has not approved those names for the post of AG.\n\nMeanwhile, the Mahanayaka Theras last week requested the Government to consider Gammanpila for the post considering his seniority in the service."
  },
