    "md5": "05ae1f463087487de7284a37dd8ad25c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1878,
    "chunk_text": "HNB backs TiECON Sri Lanka 2026 as Platinum Sponsor\n\nHNB MD/CEO Damith Pallewatte participates in a panel discussion at the TiECON Summit\n\nHNB PLC recently backed the TiECON Sri Lanka 2026 as its Platinum Sponsor, reinforcing its commitment to supporting Sri Lankan entrepreneurs as they scale beyond local market entry and compete internationally.\n\nThrough this partnership, HNB backed a summit designed to drive practical, execution-led conversations between founders, investors, mentors, and industry leaders.\n\nHosted at Cinnamon Life, Colombo, TiECON Sri Lanka 2026 convened the ecosystem under the theme \u201cGo Global: The Runway to the World,\u201d with discussions centred on building credibility, strengthening partnerships, and creating clearer market pathways for regional and global expansion.\n\nSpeaking during TiECON\u2019s concluding panel discussion on scaling beyond market entry amid shifting trade and policy conditions, HNB Managing Director/Chief Executive Officer, Damith Pallewatte said: \u201cBanks can play a practical role in helping businesses scale beyond Sri Lanka, particularly when trade conditions and policy environments can shift quickly. We see this clearly in areas like foreign currency exposure, where companies may secure export orders but lose value because the risk is not understood or managed. Banks also support growth by helping manage payment and country risk through the right financial instruments, while using transaction insights to strengthen supply chain and cross-border capability as businesses expand.\u201d\n\nThis year\u2019s programme brought together over 600 participants and over 30 global speakers, with sessions focused on navigating shifting trade and tariff regimes, scaling from regional success to global leadership, staying relevant in the age of AI, building strong global teams, and moving from exporter to trusted global brand."
  },
