    "chunk_size_bytes": 1565,
    "chunk_text": "More Platinum partners join APB to support 2026 Annual Convention\n\nFrom left:\u00a0 Convention Chair and\u00a0 APB Senior Vice President Dilshan Perera, President Anton Arumugam, People\u2019s Leasing Chief Operating Officer Udesh Gunawardena, Deputy General Manager Operations Ranil Perera, and Head of Branding and Communications Chaminda Dharmarathne\n\nFrom left: Convention Chair and\u00a0 APB Senior Vice President Dilshan Perera, President Anton Arumugam, LankaPay CEO Channa de Silva and\u00a0 Chief Manager-Marketing Wayomi Gunathilaka\n\nFrom left: Convention Chair and\u00a0 APB Senior Vice President Dilshan Perera, President Anton Arumugam, People\u2019s Bank CEO/GM Clive Fonseka, Deputy General Manager, Commercial Credit Thushari Hewawasam,\u00a0 Deputy General Manager, Retail Banking and Overseas Customer Services W.D.A.B. Liyanagunawardana\n\nWith growing support of platinum partners, the Association of Professional Bankers (APB) Sri Lanka continues to strengthen its flagship annual convention, reinforcing Sri Lanka\u203as presence on the global professional stage.\n\nThe APB Sri Lanka President Anton Arumugam noted that the convention reflects APB\u203as ongoing commitment to continuous knowledge sharing and deepening platforms that equip members for today\u203as demands and tomorrow\u203as challenges.\n\nAligned with the theme Navigation complexity and accelerating impact through regional synergy, the convention aims to empower Sri Lankan banking professions to think beyond the island, take their place at the global table and remain relevant in an evolving international landscape."
