    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "dc92244cf0030c63b1f02453459689de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1938,
    "chunk_text": "Stop fighting,start loving\n\nWhen we are in love we usually do not fight with our partners. After marriage, however, differences emerge and spouses begin to fight. In many marriages spouses keep on arguing about the same issues. Take heart, there are ways to break that vicious cycle and make the husband and wife feel like winners.\n\nArguments may start over something very trivial. A wife may accuse her husband for always being indecisive and a hopeless spendthrift. The exchange will end up with one spouse leaving the house. After some time, both of them will feel that they had misunderstood each other. You have to consider why you keep getting into the same argument over and over again. Psychologists who study the ways married couples communicate with each other have shed some light on this problem.\n\nIn the first place, each spouse gets into arguments in order to save face or safeguard his or her image. Nobody wants to accept defeat. Then the problem begins. Sometimes you know that you are at fault, but you are not willing to accept it. Very often any attack on your self-esteem can be unbearable. Both spouses forget that they had vowed to settle their problems amicably when they got married.\n\nIn some families, spouses recycle fights. They tend to read meanings to each other\u2019s charges that may be true or imaginary. Patterns of conflict are rooted in the way you treat your spouse. On the other hand, the real cause of the argument is seldom the discontent. Some couples regularly fight by nagging each other. This has to be avoided.\n\nA wife who knew that her husband was an ardent cricket fan stopped arguing with him when she came to know that he had neglected many social events because of cricket. She also knew that he had very good qualities as a husband. Sometime later the husband too realised that he was neglecting the home front and decided to help his wife. Thereafter their marriage took a different turn."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-02-02-islandlk-4ffd6235",
    "num": "islandlk-4ffd6235",
    "date_str": "2026-02-02",
    "description": "Stop fighting,start loving",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/stop-fightingstart-loving/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
    "time_ut": 1770055680.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-02-02-islandlk-4ffd6235-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8c9bee5da1484bdc76b818d11a62bb96",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1663,
    "chunk_text": "A wife who knew that her husband was an ardent cricket fan stopped arguing with him when she came to know that he had neglected many social events because of cricket. She also knew that he had very good qualities as a husband. Sometime later the husband too realised that he was neglecting the home front and decided to help his wife. Thereafter their marriage took a different turn.\n\nBeing in love is not like falling in love. When you are in love for some time your intense feelings will undergo drastic changes. When this happens you have to move into the next stage of love by improving your commitment and deepening your affection. This may be a difficult task at the beginning, but it can be done.\n\nHowever much you love your partner, you cannot solve all the household problems. Marriage is somewhat like running a country. No head of state will be able to solve all the problems of his countrymen. In a marriage we have to accept defeat or sacrifice our beliefs. In this respect healthy couples always agree to disagree.\n\nYou cannot avoid bitter arguments in a marriage all the time. In fact, arguments are necessary to release your tension. What is more critical is how you argue. Most couples argue with each other because their daily life is not stimulating enough. Some people believe that spouses argue because they are not sexually satisfied. This is another myth. Sex comprises about 10 per cent of what is important in a marriage. However, if there is no sexual satisfaction, it may turn out to be a big issue. According to psychologists, there should be a sexual bond to make you feel that you are more than friends. You are mates \u2013 soul mates!"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
