    "chunk_text": "In any relationship the feeling of rejection, of being unaccepted or discarded can be the most painful version of not getting what you want from the other partner. You may be rejected for a variety of reasons. Some rejections are bigger than others. They can range from a simple no to a snub or a betrayal. Psychologists advise people to think of rejection as God\u2019s protection. Try to find the meaning of a rejection in a wider context.\n\nAnother factor is that wives spend far more time than their husbands ruminating about upsetting encounters. Troubles in a close relationship such as marriage drive adverse biological reactions in wives more strongly than in husbands. Much of the tension in a marriage can be lessened by touching the body of your spouse passionately. When you do so, oxytocin releases making the body to undergo a host of healthy changes. Even your blood pressure will lower as you slide into a relaxed mode of parasympathetic activity.\n\nAlthough arguments, counter arguments and conflicts are inevitable in any marriage, husbands and wives should be able to cope with them and lead a happy married life.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
