    "chunk_size_bytes": 906,
    "chunk_text": "Executive President, Office of the Attorney General and public trust doctrine\n\nThe Constitution of Sri Lanka and Executive Presidential system was adopted on 7 September 1978 and the Code of Criminal Procedure Code Act (CCrPC) was enacted on 2 July 1979. The CCPrC was a measure to deal with the broad issues of the criminal justice system which postulates broad powers to the Office of the Attorney General. The Supreme Law of the Country is the Constitution. The provisions of the CCrP have not been challenged in the Supreme Court by the civil society or by the Bar Association of Sri Lanka. The writer has examined the first volume of the Parliament of Sri Lanka (https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/scdecisions/sc-decisions-on-parliamentary-bills-1978-1983-volume-i.pdf) and it seems the Act had been enacted without a challenge. The ignorance of civil society at that time must be questioned."
