    "md5": "c0bf6740806243852ab75c95c38234ce",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1964,
    "chunk_text": "SLAEA AGM reappoints Rajitha Jayasuriya as Chair\n\nThe Sri Lanka Apparel Exporters Association (SLAEA) held its Annual General Meeting on 27 January 2026 at Cinnamon Life, bringing together industry leaders, policymakers and the diplomatic community to review sector priorities and reinforce Sri Lanka\u2019s position in global apparel supply chains.\n\nAt the AGM, Rajitha Jayasuriya was reappointed as Chairperson for a second term, alongside the newly appointed Executive Committee comprising Jeevith Senaratne as Deputy Chairperson, Hasib Omar as Treasurer, and Indika Liyanahewage as Immediate Past Chairperson.\n\nIn her address, Jayasuriya pointed to the sector\u2019s resilience in 2025, noting that apparel exports grew by 5.42% to reach $ 5.019 billion, with exports to the European Union rising 12.48% and non-traditional markets recording a 4.8% increase.\n\n\u201cAs we work to expand in Europe, the renewal of GSP+ must be treated as a national priority, because it protects momentum and safeguards access to one of our most important growing markets. With India having sealed its FTA with the EU, we will need to mobilise faster, to ensure Sri Lanka is not left behind,\u201d she stressed.\n\nShe also called for a wider competitiveness agenda beyond market access, including a dedicated trade office to prioritise key FTAs, faster export facilitation through the Single Window system and ETA, predictable fiscal administration including VAT refunds, and accelerated digital reforms such as the move towards a fiscalised e-invoicing system, building on the ongoing industry pilot integrating an API with RAMIS 2.0.\n\nThe AGM was attended by Chief Guest Acting Indian High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Dr. Satyanjal Pandey, representing High Commissioner Santosh Jha, and Guest of Honour Oniverse Group Founder Dr. Sandro Veronesi. Proceedings included remarks by the Chief Guest and Guest of Honour, the Chairperson\u2019s address, and the launch of SLAEA\u2019s revamped website."
  },
