    "chunk_size_bytes": 1949,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Trevor Mendis joins Odel Board\n\nOdel PLC has appointed Dr. Trevor Mendis to its Board as an Independent Non-Executive Director.\n\nHe is a strategist, management consultant, banker, and a pracedamic who blends his wealth of hands-on local and global exposure into the corporate world. Presently he works as Senior Management Consultant and a Member of the Board of Study for the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM), University of Sri Jayewardenepura.\n\nFrom humble beginnings as a Junior Banker, Dr. Mendis rose up in the ranks to Assistant General Manager, Corporate Planning and Business Development and Leasing in the banking industry. He has also worked at ANZ Bank, New Zealand, a Fortune 500 Company and was a member of the Strategic Planning Committee at ANZ bank for the North Shore Region of Auckland, New Zealand.\n\nHe shifted from banking to the consultancy and academic arena in 2008 and became the Chief Executive Officer of a private university in Sri Lanka. Since then, Dr. Mendis\u2019 corporate and academic career trajectory has been phenomenal and impressive. He served as an External Consultant for the United Nations (Intl Trade Centre of Geneva) on two occasions and as a Lead Consultant for the Asian Development Bank (ADB) on many occasions in Sri Lanka. He was head hunted by the UN and the ADB on all these occasions.\n\nHe has served as a Non-Executive Director and the Chairman of the Strategic Direction Committee of the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation in 2019 purely on merit. He has been bestowed with two international awards in Singapore and India on merit for his achievements.\n\nHe was a member of the Final Panel of Judges for the annual awards organized by the Institute of Chartered Accountants and National Business Excellence Awards organized by the National Chamber of Commerce (NCC). He has addressed Research Conferences as the International Guest Speaker and Chief Guest both locally and internationally."
  },
