    "md5": "6ddc96381f0372c297d13d073649357d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 798,
    "chunk_text": "Indian HC responds to alleged assaults on SL fishermen\n\nThe Indian High Commission yesterday issued a statement regarding the assaults on Sri Lankan fishermen at sea allegedly by Indian personnel.\n\nIn the statement, it was acknowledged that they had seen media reports of Sri Lankan fishermen assaulted at sea on 29 January.\n\n\u201cWe have ascertained and can confirm that no such assault was inflicted by any Indian Navy or Indian Coast Guard personnel,\u201d it noted.\n\nThe statement added that India has consistently maintained that a humanitarian approach should be adopted to fishermen\u2019s livelihood concerns and that the use of force should not be resorted to under any circumstance.\n\n\u201cWe continue to be in touch with the Government of Sri Lanka on these matters,\u201d the High Commission assured."
