    "description": "Aban Pestonjee honoured with Lifetime Achievement Award at SLID-ACCA National Director Awards",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Aban-Pestonjee-honoured-with-Lifetime-Achievement-Award-at-SLID-ACCA-National-Director-Awards/34-788013",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1770403621.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-02-07-dailyftlk-9e8f2851-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "53998b075454ab4115dc9a911ecd3942",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1934,
    "chunk_text": "Aban Pestonjee honoured with Lifetime Achievement Award at SLID-ACCA National Director Awards\n\nFrom left: IFC Principal Country Officer Victor Pillai, SLID Chairman Dinesh Weerakkody, Abans Group Chairperson Aban Pestonjee, British High Commissioner Andrew Patrick, SEC Chairman Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, and ACCA in South Asia Head Nilusha Ranasinghe\n\nAbans Group of Companies Chairperson and Founder Aban Pestonjee was awarded the Lifetime Achievement award at the inaugural SLID\u2013ACCA National Corporate Director Awards 2025, hosted by the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID), in partnership with ACCA on 28 January at the Cinnamon Grand Colombo.\n\nThe event sought to recognise and celebrate outstanding corporate directors who have demonstrated leadership, integrity, and governance excellence, while shaping the future of Sri Lankan business. This initiative also marks a significant milestone in strengthening board professionalism and promoting global best practices in corporate governance.\n\nWith over four decades of experience in the business world, Pestonjee\u2019s vision, leadership and entrepreneurial spirit have been instrumental in driving the growth and success of the Abans Group. An embodiment of the company\u2019s ethos of \u2018identifying a need and fulfilling it\u2019, her passion, drive and courage as a South Asian woman in a male-dominated business world have served as an inspiration to subsequent generations of Sri Lankan businesswomen.\n\nSpeaking to the World Bank blog \u201cEnd Poverty in South Asia\u201d, compiled by experts focused on improving lives and bringing opportunities to South Asia, Pestonjee also spoke on the extensive steps she had taken throughout her career that made her deserving of the title \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s Top Women Entrepreneur\u201d. She said that the winning formula lies in none other than three cornerstone principles that defined her life: Honesty, Hard work and Perseverance."
  },
