    "chunk_size_bytes": 1291,
    "chunk_text": "Speaking to the World Bank blog \u201cEnd Poverty in South Asia\u201d, compiled by experts focused on improving lives and bringing opportunities to South Asia, Pestonjee also spoke on the extensive steps she had taken throughout her career that made her deserving of the title \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s Top Women Entrepreneur\u201d. She said that the winning formula lies in none other than three cornerstone principles that defined her life: Honesty, Hard work and Perseverance.\n\nIn 2021, she was recognised as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most admired leaders at the Most Admired Companies Awards, organised by the International Chamber of Commerce Sri Lanka and the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants. Pestonjee has also been interviewed by The Harvard Business School, and the transcript of the interview is held in the school\u2019s Baker Library, available to students for research and case studies.\n\nAs the national body dedicated to advancing director professionalism, SLID believes that recognising governance excellence is critical to building resilient institutions, attracting quality investment, and enhancing national credibility. The partnership with ACCA brings global stature to the awards, reinforcing the link between sound governance, financial stewardship, and sustainable value creation."
